-- Plan 64 leaf 5: the six retired spellings, and the diagnostic that is the
-- migration guide.
--
-- `print` appeared in 29 of the 31 examples, so this message is the only
-- thing a reader of an older program will see — plan 52's, 57's, 59's and
-- 60's choice, applied a fifth time and now the milestone's standing answer
-- to a retired spelling.
--
-- Read in **prefix** position, where a bare name is a value: `println!` has
-- already been taken by the macro branch, and `.print` and `x.print` are a
-- method reference and a field. What is left is a name standing where the
-- six retired constructs stood.
--
-- `assert` is the only one of the six that was a reserved word. The other
-- five were emitter special cases on an ordinary call, which is why this is a
-- parser diagnostic rather than a lexer one — and why `print` is still in
-- `leaves_ordinary_identifiers_alone`.

main : ()
main =
  print "hello"
  ()
